1
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:01,000
David Attenborough: A Life on Our Planet is a documentary,
drama film directed by Alastair Fothergill.

2
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:56,000
The story of life on our planet by the man who has seen
more of the natural world than any other.

3
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:51,000
In more than 90 years, Attenborough has visited every continent on the globe, exploring the wild
places of our planet and documenting the living world in all its variety and wonder.

4
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Addressing the biggest challenges facing life on our planet, the film
offers a powerful message of hope for future generations.

5
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Self, played by David Attenborough.

6
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Young David, played by Max Hughes.

7
00:48:25,000 --> 00:48:31,000
David Attenborough: A Life on Our Planet is a 2020 British documentary film narrated
by David Attenborough and produced and directed by Jonnie Hughes.

8
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:26,000
The film acts as a "witness statement", through which Attenborough shares first-hand his concern for the
current state of the planet due to humanity's impact on nature and his hopes for the future.

9
01:02:15,000 --> 01:02:21,000
It was released on Netflix on 4 October 2020, along with
a companion book A Life on Our Planet.

10
01:09:10,000 --> 01:09:16,000
The film explores themes of climate change, biography,
destruction of planet, nature, evolution.

11
01:16:05,000 --> 01:16:11,000
The tone is emotional.
